# Software Requirements Specification
## The Lenny Growth Assistant

**Version:** 1.0
**Document type:** SRS (IEEE 830-style, adapted)

---

## 1. Introduction

### 1.1 Purpose
This document specifies the functional and non-functional requirements for **The Lenny Growth Assistant**, a full-stack, AI-powered conversational web application that ingests transcripts from Lenny's Podcast, answers product-management and growth questions grounded strictly in that content, generates Ship30for30-style formatted essays on demand, and renders generated Markdown/HTML artifacts in an in-app viewer.

### 1.2 Scope
The system consists of:
- A **FastAPI** backend exposing session, chat, and artifact endpoints
- A **Postgres** database (Supabase or Railway) persisting sessions, messages, and artifacts
- An **LLM abstraction layer** supporting both a cloud provider (Anthropic Claude, accessed via the **Anthropic Claude SDK**, not a raw HTTP wrapper) and a local provider (Ollama), switchable via configuration through a common provider interface (see §3, FR-2)
- A **knowledge base** built from Lenny's Podcast transcripts, queried via retrieval-augmented generation (RAG)
- Three **skills**: Q&A (grounded retrieval), Ship30for30 content generation, and Artifact generation
- A **frontend** with a chat interface and a side-by-side Artifact Viewer that renders generated Markdown and HTML/CSS natively (not as raw code)

Out of scope: multi-user authentication/authorization, billing, mobile apps, ingestion of the full transcript corpus in real time (batch ingestion is acceptable), fine-tuning of any model.

### 1.3 Definitions
| Term | Meaning |
|---|---|
| Skill | An independent, provider-agnostic module with its own prompt/instructions that the router can invoke (Q&A, Ship30for30, Artifact) |
| Artifact | A discrete Markdown document or HTML/CSS snippet generated by the agent, stored and rendered separately from the chat transcript |
| Session | A single conversation thread with its own message history and context, analogous to a ChatGPT "chat" |
| Provider | An interchangeable LLM backend implementing a common interface — the cloud provider wraps the **Anthropic Claude SDK** (`anthropic` Python package), the local provider wraps the Ollama client/HTTP API |
| Grounded answer | A response whose factual content is derived only from retrieved transcript chunks, not model prior knowledge |

