## 2. Overall Description

### 2.1 Product Perspective
A standalone web application with a decoupled frontend (SPA) and backend (REST API). The backend owns all LLM calls, retrieval, and persistence; the frontend is a thin client rendering chat and artifacts.

### 2.2 User Classes
| User class | Description | Needs |
|---|---|---|
| Evaluator/end user | Asks growth/PM questions, requests content, inspects artifacts | Fast, grounded answers; readable artifacts; ability to start fresh sessions |
| Operator/developer | Runs the app locally with own API keys and Ollama | Clear config, provider toggle, error visibility |

### 2.3 Assumptions and Dependencies
- An Anthropic API key is available for the cloud path.
- Ollama is installed and running locally with at least one pulled model for the local path.
- A Postgres instance (Supabase or Railway) is reachable and has the required extensions (`pgvector` if used).
- The transcript source repository is publicly accessible at build/ingestion time.

