## 6. Acceptance Criteria Summary

| Requirement | Acceptance test |
|---|---|
| FR-1 | Create two sessions, send different messages to each, confirm no cross-contamination of context; run a long session past the context threshold and confirm graceful truncation/summarization instead of an error |
| FR-2 | Toggle provider config; confirm both the Claude SDK path and the Ollama path independently produce a valid response to the same prompt via the same factory-constructed interface; confirm streaming output appears incrementally where supported |
| FR-3/FR-4 | Ask an in-corpus question → grounded answer with source attribution visibly displayed (not just logged); ask an out-of-corpus question → explicit refusal/deflection, not fabrication; swap the configured embedding model and confirm retrieval still functions |
| FR-5 | Request Ship30for30 output → word count in range, contains hook, bullets, bold text, a closing takeaway, and reads as conversational/narrative rather than a bulleted summary of facts |
| FR-6/FR-7 | Confirm each skill runs correctly when invoked directly with a provider, independent of the router; send an ambiguous message and a context-dependent follow-up ("now make that a post") and confirm the routing log shows correct intent + context-based classification in each case |
| FR-8/FR-9 | Generate a Markdown artifact and an HTML artifact in the same session → both render correctly in the viewer without a page reload or external redirect; toggle to raw source view and confirm the underlying code is shown accurately |

